          "heading": "Félix Páez Molina hails 2035 bid as vital for South American rugby",
          "body": "Argentine Rugby Union president Félix Páez Molina has described the joint South American bid for the 2035 Rugby World Cup as a \"very important step\" for the region. Argentina are leading a four-nation consortium alongside Brazil, Chile and Uruguay, with technical information now submitted to World Rugby. The proposal includes 11 venues, such as the Estadio Monumental in Buenos Aires and the Maracanã in Rio de Janeiro. This first-ever South American bid faces competition from Spain, Italy and Japan, with a final decision expected in November 2027."
